cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the analyses in this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Mapping the Phenotypic Landscape of Beta-lactam Resistance in Streptococcus pneumoniae"
abstract: >-
  Code and analysis workflows for the paper above, which introduces Antimicrobial
  Resistance (AMR) Cartography, a
  multidimensional-scaling and multivariate linear mixed model framework for
  analysing continuous, correlated minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC)
  profiles, applied to beta-lactam resistance in Streptococcus pneumoniae.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AndrewBalmer/AMR-cartography"
keywords:
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - Streptococcus pneumoniae
  - beta-lactams
  - multidimensional scaling
  - multivariate linear mixed models
  - penicillin-binding proteins
